TL;DR: Short but really fun 4-player hack&slash dungeon crawler co-op. If it's on sale it's a pretty good buy to play with friends if you enjoy this type of games.
Haven't played previous Gauntlet games, but on its own it's a fun game with smooth and polished controls and combat that offers an interesting and enjoyable experience with friends.
The campaign is way too short so I wouldn't really recommend buying the game unless it's on sale, but defenitely worth a buy then. Replayability may come in trying the game on a higher difficulty and/or re-playing with a different character.
Customization is not much, but allows for some variation in each character's playstyle as chosing certain weapons and items will replace some abilities with others.
Pros:
- Fun and smooth 4player co-op;
- Rewarding action-packed hack&slash combat;
- Different characters with unique gameplay each;
- Game divided in short to medium levels means you can play even in short-sessions if you wish;
Cons:
- Too short - Depending on your team pacing and the difficulty you will probably clear the main game in around 6 hours or so;
- Weird difficulty curve - Many levels in the middle of the game feel easier and much shorter (some feel quite rushed) than some of the initial ones (they do become harder and longer later on);
Overall it's worth a buy if it's on sale and it's a type game you and 3 other friends enjoy.

