When I started playing this game, I didn't know what to expect from it. I thought of a wonky game, which I would play for a few hours and just quit after. What I got out of it in the last two weeks, has just been amazing gameplay. The game feels smooth and very balanced. Playing a diver is fun, but not overpowered. Same thing when playing the shark. It also gives off a feel which I had with cs:go. That is that you improve with the weapons, not let the weapons improve. So, as a quick run-down:
Positives:
- Smooth gameplay;
- A very balanced game;
- A 'you improve' type of feel;
- (Note, maybe not something for you) free skins!
- A mildly cheap game;
- The game isn't dead;
- A game which can be a lot of fun, singleplayer or multiplayer.
Negatives:
- The case system (You can get cases for free, though.);
- Mildly toxic community.
If you see this game on a sale, I would recommend to give it a try. You might like it as much as I did already.

